Requirements: 55   with obligations: 54   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Make decomposition incremental over recorded state. A requirement whose text
    did not change keeps the obligations already derived from it, and costs no model
    call. A requirement that was edited is re-derived from what it was and what it
    became; one that is new is derived fresh; one that disappeared has its obligations
    dropped.
    -> incremental-decomposition-over-recorded-state  [functional/explicit]
       Decomposition is incremental over recorded state: unchanged requirements keep
       their previously derived obligations without a model call; edited requirements
       are re-derived from prior text, new text, and prior obligations; new requirements
       are derived fresh; disappeared requirements have their obligations dropped.

[task-02] Each run identifies itself and records what it derived, so that a later run
    can name it as the run it continues.
    -> run-identifies-itself-and-records-derivations  [functional/explicit]
       Each run identifies itself and records what it derived so that a later run can
       name it as the run it continues.

[constraint-01] A requirement whose text is unchanged from the continued run causes no
    model call during decomposition.
    -> unchanged-requirement-no-model-call  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement whose text is unchanged from the continued run causes no model call
       during decomposition.

[constraint-02] The obligations of an unchanged requirement are carried forward with
    their identifiers unchanged.
    -> unchanged-requirement-carry-forward-identifiers  [invariant/explicit]
       The obligations of an unchanged requirement are carried forward with their
       identifiers unchanged.

[constraint-03] The obligations of an unchanged requirement are carried forward with
    their descriptions unchanged.
    -> unchanged-requirement-carry-forward-descriptions  [invariant/explicit]
       The obligations of an unchanged requirement are carried forward with their
       descriptions unchanged.

[constraint-04] An edited requirement is re-derived in one model call carrying the
    previous text, the new text, and the obligations previously derived from that
    requirement.
    -> edited-requirement-single-rederive-call  [functional/explicit]
       An edited requirement is re-derived in one model call carrying the previous text,
       the new text, and the obligations previously derived from that requirement.

[constraint-05] An obligation that persists across an edit to its requirement keeps the
    identifier it already had.
    -> persisting-obligation-keeps-identifier-across-edit  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation that persists across an edit to its requirement keeps the
       identifier it already had.

[constraint-06] A requirement present in the continued run and absent from the task file
    under review has its obligations dropped.
    -> drop-obligations-for-removed-requirement  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement present in the continued run and absent from the task file under
       review has its obligations dropped.

[constraint-07] The removal of such a requirement is reported.
    -> report-removal-of-missing-requirement  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The removal of such a requirement is reported.

[constraint-08] A requirement with no counterpart in the continued run is derived
    without reference to any previously derived obligation.
    -> derive-new-requirement-freshly  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement with no counterpart in the continued run is derived without
       reference to any previously derived obligation.

[constraint-09] Two requirements are the same requirement when their text matches
    exactly.
    -> exact-text-match-defines-same-requirement  [invariant/explicit]
       Two requirements are the same requirement when their text matches exactly.

[constraint-10] Requirements left unmatched by exact text are matched to each other
    through `benchmark/alignment.py::align_obligations`, which distinguishes an edited
    requirement from a new one.
    -> align-unmatched-requirements-by-alignment-helper  [functional/explicit]
       Requirements left unmatched by exact text are matched to each other through
       `benchmark/alignment.py::align_obligations`, which distinguishes an edited
       requirement from a new one.

[constraint-11] A merge decision over two obligations that are both unchanged is carried
    forward without a model call.
    -> carry-forward-unchanged-merge-decisions  [functional/explicit]
       A merge decision over two obligations that are both unchanged is carried forward
       without a model call.

[constraint-12] A merge decision over two obligations of which either changed is asked
    again.
    -> reask-merge-decision-when-either-obligation-changed  [functional/explicit]
       A merge decision over two obligations of which either changed is asked again.

[constraint-13] Carry-forward reads only the run named as the continued run.
    -> carry-forward-reads-only-continued-run  [invariant/explicit]
       Carry-forward reads only the run named as the continued run.

[constraint-14] No obligation is carried forward when no continued run is named.
    -> no-carry-forward-without-continued-run  [invariant/explicit]
       No obligation is carried forward when no continued run is named.

[constraint-15] A carried obligation's `source_quote` is an exact substring of its
